From 2f52ca491cadce9521acb864bfe31d26f38217d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 03:47:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] repack: fix the shadow tensor COUNT in the accounting line,
 and strengthen the claim it supports

The byte totals were right; the counts were not, and one of them was load-bearing for a claim.

The INFO accounting line printed `g_arifi_dual_shadows.size() + 1`, but the record is emplaced
just above it - so every model reported one shadow more than it had ("2 tensors so far" on the
first). The harness compounded it by matching "CPU_REPACK_DUAL shadow", which catches the
running-total INFO lines as well as the per-tensor rows. Together they made the shadow count read
169/73/5 against mode 1's 168/72/4 on the three models.

Neither was an extra shadow. Reconciled against the per-tensor rows: DEBUG lines and DISTINCT
TENSOR NAMES are 4 / 72 / 168 on the three models, exactly mode 1's tensor set. That is a stronger
check than the byte totals matching, which is what FINDINGS and the registry claimed - both now
say so, and both record the two reporting defects rather than quietly correcting the number.

Rebuilt and re-judged: F-085 PASS (" Paris." on the ternary g128 27B).

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110E, follow-up
Measured-effect: none on any code path - the changed line is a log format string. The claim it
  supports is now verified by tensor name rather than inferred from byte totals.
---
 docs/FINDINGS.md             | 5 +++--
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md     | 2 +-
 ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

